  {
    "number": 13,
    "title": "Implement selective 3-of-6 challenge protocol",
    "body": "## Summary\n\n- add uniform and alternating-halves challenge schedulers with stable active-challenge state\n- add the pressed-keys-plus-one selective tower shuffle for 6-key by 8-icon layouts\n- make successful advancement idempotent across duplicate finish races\n- compare both schedules with paired, domain-separated benchmark trials\n- expand JSON, CSV, Markdown, and chart artifacts with scheduling and selective-shuffle metrics\n\n## Validation\n\n- `git diff --check`\n- `python -m py_compile src/challenge_schedule.py src/challenge_protocol.py src/keypad/keypad.py src/challenge_subset.py cli/challenge_subset_benchmark.py`\n- `python -m pytest -q` (48 passed)\n- default two-schedule CLI smoke run (20 paired scenarios)\n- single-schedule CLI smoke run (`alternating-halves`)\n- existing 6x8 4-of-4 crack/replay regression remains exactly four observations",
